.TH SYSTEMD-SENTRY.SERVICE 8 "September 2026" "systemd-sentry 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
systemd-sentry.service, sentry.service, systemd-sentry.socket, sentry.socket \- systemd supervisor service and socket units
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B systemctl
start systemd-sentry.service
.br
.B systemctl
enable --now systemd-sentry.socket
.br
.B systemctl
status sentry.service
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B systemd-sentry.service
runs the background autonomous supervisor for systemd units.
.PP
The service operates under a heavily sandboxed environment with strict privilege
separation and Linux kernel security features:
.IP \(bu 2
Runs as dedicated non-root system user \fIsentry\fR (provisioned via
.BR sysusers.d (5)).
.IP \(bu 2
Member of \fIsystemd-journal\fR group for journal stream ingestion.
.IP \(bu 2
Drops all kernel capabilities except \fICAP_DAC_READ_SEARCH\fR (reading journal
and cgroup structures) and \fICAP_KILL\fR (sending signals).
.IP \(bu 2
Strict read-only filesystem via \fIProtectSystem=strict\fR, isolating home
directories with \fIProtectHome=yes\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
Only writable directories are \fI/run/systemd-sentry\fR,
\fI/var/log/systemd-sentry\fR, and \fI/var/lib/systemd-sentry\fR (provisioned
via
.BR tmpfiles.d (5)).
.IP \(bu 2
Memory execution protection via \fIMemoryDenyWriteExecute=yes\fR.
.SH SOCKET ACTIVATION
.B systemd-sentry.socket
listens on \fI/run/systemd-sentry/sentry.sock\fR. When systemd activates the
service, the listening file descriptor is passed to the process at descriptor 3
using the standard \fI$LISTEN_FDS\fR protocol.
.SH WATCHDOG
The service integrates with systemd's software watchdog mechanism. The daemon
periodically emits \fIWATCHDOG=1\fR state datagrams to \fI$NOTIFY_SOCKET\fR at
half the configured \fIWatchdogSec\fR interval (every 7.5 seconds when
\fIWatchdogSec=15s\fR).
.PP
If the supervisor process deadlocks, hangs, or fails to service the watchdog,
systemd will automatically kill and restart the service according to
\fIRestart=always\fR.
.SH INTEGRATIONS
.TP
.B systemd-coredump
The supervisor monitors crash signals (\fISIGSEGV\fR, \fISIGABRT\fR). When a
coredump is generated, the supervisor parses extended attributes
(\fIuser.coredump.*\fR) on files in \fI/var/lib/systemd/coredump/\fR without
reading the entire binary core into RAM.
.TP
.B systemd-oomd
Under high memory pressure, out-of-memory kills initiated by \fIsystemd-oomd\fR
or the kernel OOM killer are detected via D-Bus failure reasons
(\fIResult=oom-kill\fR) and cgroup v2 \fImemory.events\fR counters.
.TP
.B systemd-creds
API keys and authentication secrets can be securely provisioned to the service
using
.BR systemd-creds (1)
encrypted against the TPM2 chip or host credentials. The daemon automatically
discovers secrets mounted into \fI$CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd-sentry (1),
.BR systemd-sentry.conf (5),
.BR systemd.service (5),
.BR systemd.socket (5),
.BR systemd-creds (1),
.BR systemd-oomd.service (8)
